Third-party terms
=================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the SOURCE CODE in this repository:
everything under src/, scripts/, server/, deploy/, and the build configuration.

It does not cover the material below, which is not ours to relicense.


Data committed in this repository
---------------------------------

public/data/ holds roughly 5 MB of third-party data, each with its own terms:

  public/data/MM_*/            Flood extents and exposure, derived from UNOSAT
                               products obtained via HDX. CC BY-SA.
                               https://data.humdata.org/organization/unosat

  Region boundaries            Used during conversion to clip extents to
                               regions. geoBoundaries, ODbL.
                               https://www.geoboundaries.org/

  Impact figures               WFP ADAM. CC BY-SA.
                               https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org

Redistributing that data means honouring those licences, not the MIT one. In
particular, CC BY-SA is a share-alike licence and an MIT file at the root of a
repository cannot override it.


Data fetched at run time
------------------------

The served page contacts these directly; none of it is covered by LICENSE:

  NASA GIBS                    Satellite imagery and GPM IMERG rainfall.
  Open-Meteo                   Rainfall forecasts. CC BY 4.0.
  GloFAS / Copernicus EMS      River discharge forecasts.
  OpenStreetMap / OpenFreeMap  Basemap. ODbL.
  EOX Sentinel-2 cloudless     The "Cloud-free" basemap. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

The last one is easy to get wrong: EOX Sentinel-2 cloudless is NON-COMMERCIAL,
and that restriction applies to anything using that basemap whatever LICENSE
says about this project's code.


